1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,899
Nigeria goes to the polls in January 2027.

2
00:00:05,949 --> 00:00:11,049
Here's what you need to know about the general elections, in under three minutes.

3
00:00:11,799 --> 00:00:13,955
There are two election days.

4
00:00:14,005 --> 00:00:20,726
On Saturday 16 January, Nigerians vote for the President and the National Assembly.

5
00:00:20,776 --> 00:00:27,071
Three weeks later, on 6 February, they vote for governors and state Houses of Assembly.

6
00:00:27,821 --> 00:00:30,894
These dates are earlier than first planned.

7
00:00:30,944 --> 00:00:36,108
INEC originally fixed 20 February for the presidential vote.

8
00:00:36,158 --> 00:00:46,122
It revised the calendar after President Tinubu signed the Electoral Act 2026 in February 2026.

9
00:00:46,872 --> 00:00:56,857
On day one, voters choose a President, all 109 Senators and all 360 members of the House of Representatives.

10
00:00:56,907 --> 00:01:04,418
On day two, 28 states elect a governor, and all 36 states elect their Houses of Assembly.

11
00:01:04,468 --> 00:01:10,272
The other eight states hold governorship elections on their own, off-cycle calendar.

12
00:01:11,022 --> 00:01:14,223
How does a candidate win the presidency?

13
00:01:14,273 --> 00:01:17,069
They need the most votes nationwide.

14
00:01:17,119 --> 00:01:24,331
And at least 25% of the vote in at least two-thirds of the states and the FCT.

15
00:01:24,381 --> 00:01:28,244
If nobody clears that bar, a second round is held.

16
00:01:28,994 --> 00:01:33,454
Eighteen candidates are on INEC's final presidential list.

17
00:01:33,504 --> 00:01:50,721
In alphabetical order, they include Atiku Abubakar (ADC), Donald Duke (PRP), Seyi Makinde (APM), Peter Obi (NDC), Sandy Onor (PDP) and President Bola Tinubu (APC).

18
00:01:50,771 --> 00:01:53,951
Two of the 18 candidates are women.

19
00:01:54,701 --> 00:02:01,700
On election day, accreditation and voting run from 8:30 am to 2:30 pm.

20
00:02:01,750 --> 00:02:04,226
Bring your Permanent Voter Card.

21
00:02:04,276 --> 00:02:08,032
Your identity is checked on the BVAS machine.

22
00:02:08,082 --> 00:02:13,950
Results from each polling unit can then be viewed on INEC's online results portal.

23
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:19,032
By the numbers: more than 93 million registered voters.

24
00:02:19,082 --> 00:02:23,435
More than 176,000 polling units.

25
00:02:23,485 --> 00:02:27,156
And 22 registered political parties.

26
00:02:27,906 --> 00:02:31,833
So, find your polling unit. Collect your PVC.

27
00:02:31,883 --> 00:02:37,836
And before you share a rumour about the election, check it against INEC's official channels.

28
00:02:37,886 --> 00:02:43,221
Your vote. Your voice. 16 January 2027.

